# Frontend Production Environment Variables

# The backend API this build talks to.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite bakes this value into the bundle at BUILD time, not run time.
# Changing it means you must run `npm run build` again and redeploy — editing it
# on the server does nothing.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE. The contact endpoint now ships with the site as a Vercel
# serverless function at /api/contact, so requests are same-origin: the browser
# asks the very host it loaded the page from. That removes the two failure modes
# that killed every previous setup — a cross-origin request CORS could reject,
# and an http:// API that an https:// page refuses to call.
#
# History of this value (all of these are dead, and none need reviving):
#   https://techland-backend.onrender.com  - Render service unreachable
#   http://147.93.27.247:5000              - Hostinger VPS, all ports closed
#   https://apis.techlanditsolutions.com   - DNS -> the same dead VPS
#
# Set this to a full https:// origin ONLY if the API moves back onto its own
# host — for example once the full Express backend is deployed for the Admin
# panel. Leave it empty while /api lives beside the site.
VITE_API_URL=
